<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31763" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ŏb-ŏlĕo</span></b> ,
			ŭi, 2, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to smell of</i> any thing
			(ante-class. and post-Aug.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oboluisti allium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Most. 1, 1, 38</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">maluissem allium oboluisses,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Vesp. 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">antidotum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Calig. 23</span></i>
			: res mihi obolet. <i>I smell a thing</i>,
					<i><span class="en">App. Mag. p. 311,
			31</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jam oboluit Casina procul,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cas. 4, 3, 21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">marsupium huic oboluit,</span>”
				<i>she smells your purse</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Men. 2, 3, 33</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
